  "notes": "2.9.11: less 710-1. /etc/profile exports PAGER=less and cixctl pages through less, and no less package existed until now (cix#378, 2026-10-31). 2.9.10: curl 8.21.0-7, whose CA bundle is explicit (cix#589). 8.21.0-6 had no compiled-in bundle, so curl here fell back to OpenSSL's /usr/lib/ssl, which holds no certificates, and every HTTPS fetch failed with unable to get local issuer certificate (measured in agent-1, same package set, 2026-10-31). 2.9.9: nss-pam-ldapd 0.9.13-13 and openldap-client 2.6.14-7, built with gcc. The tcc build placed libnss_ldap's thread-local data at local-exec TLS offsets, which alias the TLS of every program that looks up a user (cix#652), and gcc cannot link tcc-built liblber.a. 2.9.8 named nss-pam-ldapd 0.9.13-9, which failed to build; its libuuid 2.42.2-8 stays.",
